{"id": "EUVD-2026-103838", "enisaUuid": "efd40fbf-2875-3bb8-9f4e-e1f40d10eaff", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntty: tty_port: restore TTY_IO_ERROR on activation failure\n\nMake sure to restore the TTY_IO_ERROR flag if activation fails to\nprevent I/O attempts on a port that is gone or powered down.\n\nThis specifically avoids issues like kernel panic due to unclocked\naccesses or NULL-pointer dereferences when accessing powered down or\nderegistered ports when a TTY ioctl races with hangup and open.\n\nNote that the flag is set again in tty_port_close() but not restoring it\non activation failure leaves a window where drivers fail to handle the\nioctl-hangup race.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:28", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16032c980d8f71642fcdc99309c571df3fcf3328", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/34d4f67472ef7a744970b772a8565ddc727788e2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7021acc84c2e0add77a1a33152e3a1e428fdbfdb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6388409b711eb91b14fa075a4d861ccc4df1cfe7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56964f6a31238fb41d5830bb42520c5b10ff7d8f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fxvh-5c26-7p3q", "CVE-2026-98753"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1074a8d1-ac45-303a-bb79-486917486b8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9a37ec33a1b3e66b260ac1c29bff0aec8b89ae4 <34d4f67472ef7a744970b772a8565ddc727788e2"}, {"id": "2e5b6e01-3fd9-30f5-9093-4a6a1a6d51bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9a37ec33a1b3e66b260ac1c29bff0aec8b89ae4 <7021acc84c2e0add77a1a33152e3a1e428fdbfdb"}, {"id": "45a3fbd5-c3c4-3aee-a272-25fee89104a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "521e9253-8e85-35d0-9c14-7f73417d1ba5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "